{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 750,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What would happen if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583,
    "dDurationMs": 2737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a star exploded near the earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4320,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the nearest star to\nEarth, of course, is the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7230,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is not going to explode,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9510,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if it had eight times the mass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12270,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it would go supernova\nat the end of its life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15810,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what would that look like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17580,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, as noted by xkcd if you held up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20970,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a hydrogen bomb right to your\neyeball and detonated it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25350,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that explosion would still be\na billion times less bright"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30120,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than watching the sun\ngo supernova from Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's how insanely powerful\nsupernova explosions are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39600,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are the biggest\nexplosions in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42870,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we see supernovae in other galaxies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45720,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are brighter than the combined light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48180,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of hundreds of billions of\nstars, so bright, in fact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52230,
    "dDurationMs": 2523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they appear to come out of nowhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55680,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the 8th of October, 1604,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57930,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the astronomer Johannes Kepler\nlooked up into the night sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61740,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and noticed a bright star\nhe had never seen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65250,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was brighter than all\nthe other stars in the sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68850,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and about as bright as the planet Jupiter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72090,
    "dDurationMs": 3513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On moonless nights, it was\nbright enough to cast a shadow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76440,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kepler published his observations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78000,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this star in a book\ncalled \"De Stella Nova,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80850,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means \"about a new star\" in Latin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84990,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kepler thought he was witnessing\nthe birth of a new star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88860,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it was actually a\nstar's violent death."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92220,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the following year and a half,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93870,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the light faded until it\nwas no longer visible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97500,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the name stuck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99390,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even once we learned what was\nreally happening in the 1930s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102960,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the violent final explosion for stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105450,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between about 8 and 30 solar masses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107910,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been called a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111810,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how exactly a star explodes is not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114960,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what most people think."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117441,
    "dDurationMs": 3369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For most of a star's life, it\nexists in a stable balance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120810,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In its core, it fuses\nlighter elements together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123390,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make heavier ones, and in the process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125730,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it converts a small amount\nof matter into energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128910,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This energy is really what keeps the star"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131550,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from collapsing in on itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134070,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity compresses the star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136350,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that force is counteracted\nby the pressure generated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139500,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the movement of\nparticles inside the star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142410,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by the pressure of\nphotons released by fusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146220,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in effect, stars are\npropped up by their own light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152010,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the rate of fusion drops\nat the center of the star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154740,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the temperature and the pressure decrease."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157530,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity starts winning,\ncompressing the star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161010,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this increases the temperature\nand pressure in the core,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164550,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which increases the rate of fusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166890,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a stable self-regulating\nsystem, but there's a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171810,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stars have a finite amount of fuel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which over time gets used up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176640,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our sun is about 5 billion years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179070,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into its 10-billion-year lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182400,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are stars dozens of times\nmore massive than the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185730,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you would think\nwould live much longer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187830,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they actually use up\ntheir nuclear fuel faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191190,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A star 20 times the mass of our sun has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193800,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lifespan of just 10 million years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196830,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more massive stars burn\nhotter, and even brighter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200190,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but for much shorter lives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202890,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For 90% the life of a star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204900,
    "dDurationMs": 3603,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the core is only hot enough\nto fuse hydrogen into helium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209580,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when the hydrogen runs out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211020,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fusion slows, gravity compresses the core"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214350,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its temperature increases\nto 200 million degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218160,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at which point helium fuses into carbon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221190,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's enough helium to\npower the star for around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224040,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a million years, but\nas the helium runs out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227040,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the core is, again, compressed and heated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229590,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Carbon starts fusing into neon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231540,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which lasts about 1,000 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233430,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then neon fuses into\noxygen for a few more years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237600,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then oxygen to silicon for a few months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240060,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at 2.5 billion degrees, silicon fuses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into nickel which decays into iron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247080,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, at the heart of this giant star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248970,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is an iron core building that's only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252000,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few thousand kilometers across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255210,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iron is where this pattern stops."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257700,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of liberating energy as it fuses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260280,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into heavier elements, it\nactually requires energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264450,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iron is the most stable element."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267030,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it actually takes energy both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268710,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fuse it into heavier elements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270810,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to break it down into lighter ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273120,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both fusion and fission reactions\nultimately end up at iron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278640,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The iron core grows,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280500,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the crush of gravity becomes greater"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282900,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and greater as the rate of fusion drops."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the iron core is about\n1.4 times the mass of our sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289320,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is known as the\nChandrasekhar limit, the pull"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292290,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of gravity is so strong that\nsomething totally wild happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296730,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum mechanics takes over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298860,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electrons run out of room to move,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301020,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they're forced into\ntheir lowest energy states,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304350,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they then become absorbed\nby the protons in the nucleus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309210,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this process, the protons turn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311430,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into neutrons and release neutrinos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315750,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the electrons gone,\nthe core collapses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318600,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and fast, at about 25% the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322530,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what used to be a ball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323700,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of iron 3,000 kilometers\nin diameter becomes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a ball of neutrons just\n30 kilometers across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330840,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, it's a neutron star."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333660,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With no outward pressure to hold it up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336120,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rest of the star caves in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338130,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, falling at a quarter\nof the speed of flight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it hits the neutron star and bounces off,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344040,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creating a huge pressure wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346590,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this kinetic energy isn't quite enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349080,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to start a supernova explosion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351420,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, the thing that really kicks it off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353610,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the humble neutrino."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355830,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I normally think of neutrinos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357420,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as particles that do basically nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360090,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, they interact\nso rarely with matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362070,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that right now there are\n100 trillion neutrinos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365820,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "passing through your body per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368550,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would take a light year of lead just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370590,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to give you a 50-50 chance\nof stopping a neutrino,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374190,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's because they interact only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375840,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through gravity and the weak force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378690,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in a supernova, when\nthe electrons are captured"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381510,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the protons, an unbelievable number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383850,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of neutrinos is released, around 10^58."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388140,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You would think they would just fly off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390150,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at nearly the speed of light, but the core"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393000,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a supernova is incredibly dense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395430,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 10 trillion times\nmore dense than lead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399570,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as a result, it traps\nsome of those neutrinos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403380,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and captures their energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405030,
    "dDurationMs": 3401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is what makes\na star go supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408431,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A particle that is millions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410940,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of times less massive than an\nelectron that barely interacts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414570,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with anything is responsible for some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417240,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the largest explosions in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421230,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that explosion, only 1/100 of 1%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425010,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the energy is released as\nelectromagnetic radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428160,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the light that we can see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430500,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even then, supernova have enough energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432480,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to outshine a whole galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434850,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About 1% of the energy is\nreleased as the kinetic energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438390,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the exploding matter,\nbut the vast majority"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441210,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the energy is released in the form"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444210,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of neutrinos, and neutrinos are actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447600,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first signal we\ndetect from supernovae,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451410,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's because after they're generated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453570,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the core, they can escape"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456090,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the shockwave reaches the surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458850,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the light that we see is generated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461430,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So neutrinos can arrive on\nEarth hours before the photons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464910,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giving astronomers a chance\nto aim their telescopes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467640,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the right part of the sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471000,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I actually used to work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472230,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a neutrino observatory back in college,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474630,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I would work the graveyard shift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476310,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between midnight and 8:00 AM."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I detected a really big increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481080,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the neutrino flux during my shift,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482910,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was my job to call\nand wake up scientists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486090,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they could go look out for a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489000,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that never actually happened,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490560,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we did have some close calls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492960,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I need to clarify a couple things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495120,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, not all really\nmassive stars explode."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498690,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As they collapse, some\nform black holes instead,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501990,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means they do not go supernova"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504960,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and second, there's another\nway to make a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507780,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sometimes a white dwarf star,\nwhich is incredibly dense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510810,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulls matter off a nearby star,\nand when it's mass reaches"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514500,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Chandrasekhar limit\nof 1.4 solar masses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517650,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the white dwarf collapses,\ncreating a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521220,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is actually the type\nof supernova that Kepler saw"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523650,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1604, a supernova 20,000\nlight years from Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529080,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, because the shocks are asymmetric,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531930,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supernova explain neutron stars\nthat can move really fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536430,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a neutron star we've\nobserved with a velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538800,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 1,600 kilometers per second,\nand we think that was caused"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544770,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a very asymmetric supernova explosion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547860,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sent it shooting off\nin the other direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550860,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite only recently learning\nabout how supernovae work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553680,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "humans have been observing\nthem for thousands of years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557190,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ancient Indian, Chinese, Arabic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559530,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and European astronomers\nall observed supernovae,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563640,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they are quite rare."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565830,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a galaxy like our Milky Way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567750,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consisting of 100 billion stars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570150,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are only about one or\ntwo supernovae per century."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574290,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A particularly amazing example\nis the supernova of 1054,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579330,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the light of a supernova\n6,500 light years away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582930,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reached the earth and was\nrecorded by Chinese astronomers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587070,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we look to where that\nsupernova was recorded,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590010,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see the Crab Nebula."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592590,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a giant remnant\nof radioactive matter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596130,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left behind by the explosion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598530,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1,000 years since the explosion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601080,
    "dDurationMs": 3873,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the remnant has grown to\n11 light years in diameter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605970,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Supernovas produce a lot of cosmic rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608940,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cosmic rays are actually particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610830,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mainly protons and helium nuclei,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613560,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they travel out at very,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615570,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very nearly the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617550,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a tremendous amount of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620730,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at what distance could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622290,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a supernova cause problems\nfor life on Earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625257,
    "dDurationMs": 2523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The closest stars to us, besides the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627780,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the three stars in Alpha Centauri."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630540,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are 4.4 light years\naway, but stars do move around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635850,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and on average, a star\ngets within one light year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Earth every 500,000 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641160,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what would happen if\nsuch a star went off?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646290,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, so within a\nlight year, you're easily"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648600,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within a danger distance\nfrom just the kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652110,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think even at that distance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654240,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're looking at possibly\nblowing the atmosphere off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658650,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But we would also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659550,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have other problems to worry about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661380,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Supernovae create conditions\nthat are hot enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fuse elements heavier than iron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666360,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the months after the\nexplosion, these elements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669060,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "undergo radioactive decay,\nproducing gamma rays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672420,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and cosmic rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less than 0.1% of the energy produced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676680,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a supernova is emitted as gamma rays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679170,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from these radioactive decays,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680910,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but even this tiny\npercentage can be dangerous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684420,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At a few light years from a supernova,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686400,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the radiation could be deadly, though most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689730,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of it would be blocked by our atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693060,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the earth is protected\nfrom solar and cosmic radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696900,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by our atmosphere, and\nspecifically by ozone molecules,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701190,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three oxygen atoms bonded together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703830,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but high energy cosmic rays\nfrom supernova can come down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707880,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and break apart nitrogen\nmolecules in the atmosphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712290,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then these bond with oxygen atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715290,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which can then break apart ozone,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718740,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so we can lose a lot of our ozone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721740,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if there's too many cosmic rays coming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723660,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from supernova events,\nand that can expose us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to all kinds of dangerous\nradiation coming in from space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729240,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We actually see an increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730890,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in atmospheric NO3 concentrations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733110,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coinciding with supernova explosions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736620,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A supernova within 30 light years is rare,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739440,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only happening maybe once every\n1 1/2 billion years or so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743550,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a recent article suggests\nsupernovae could be lethal all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746910,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the way out to 150 light years away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750450,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so those would be much more common."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752730,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We actually have evidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754170,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a supernova that\nwent off 150 light years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756720,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from Earth 2.6 million years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759810,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would've been seen by\nour early human ancestors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762600,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Australopithecus, and we know this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765330,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there are\nelements present on Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767670,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could only have been\ndeposited by a recent supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771840,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In sedimentary rocks at the\nbottom of the Pacific Ocean,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774750,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists have found traces of iron-60,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777930,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a layer that was deposited\n2.6 million years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782070,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iron-60 is an isotope of iron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784590,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with four more neutrons than\nthe most common type of iron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788400,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iron-60 is really hard to make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790650,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our sun doesn't make it, nor\nis it produced, basically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793260,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anywhere else in the solar system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795360,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iron-60 is made, basically, exclusively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798210,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in supernova explosions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800520,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and iron-60 is radioactive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802830,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has a half life of 2.6 million years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805830,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So every 2.6 million years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807630,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "half of the sample decays into cobalt-60."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811830,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all of the iron-60 that was\naround during the formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814650,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the earth, 4.5 billion years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816870,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has definitely decayed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818910,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the iron-60 that the scientists measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821610,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is proof of a recent supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823920,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists also measured\ntrace amounts of manganese-53"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827490,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the same sediments,\ngiving further evidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829830,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supporting the idea\nthat recently there was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832080,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an explosion of a nearby supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835560,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The supernova that happened\n2.6 million years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838410,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't catastrophic for our ancestors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841200,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but some researchers hypothesized\nthat it could be related"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844290,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the mass extinction, which is seen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845940,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the Pliocene-Pleistocene boundary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848340,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the fossil record around the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851070,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This extinction wiped out\naround 1/3 of marine megafauna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855690,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea is that the cosmic rays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857610,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the supernova hit\nparticles in our atmosphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860250,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creating muons, which\nare charged particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863130,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the electron, only\nmore than 200 times heavier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866700,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The muon flux for years\nafter the supernova"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869670,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would've been 150 times\nhigher than normal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873330,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the bigger the animal, the larger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875370,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the radiation dose it would've\nreceived from these muons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878850,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why megafauna were so\ndisproportionately affected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882960,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what's more, the animals that lived"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885480,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in shallower waters were more likely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887580,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to become extinct compared to\nthe ones that lived at depth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890730,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the water would've\nprotected them from muons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894090,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Further evidence for these\nrecent nearby supernovae comes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897660,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our place in the galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900090,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, if you look in the space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901800,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the stars in\nour galaxy, on average,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904200,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are around a million\nhydrogen atoms per cubic meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908250,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That may sound like a lot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909330,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's basically a perfect vacuum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911820,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but for hundreds of light years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914370,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in all directions around our solar system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917100,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find there are 1,000\ntimes fewer hydrogen atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921510,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like they've all\nbeen blown out somewhere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924600,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and our solar system is\nexisting in this cosmic void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928500,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside a low density bubble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931200,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that is evidence for\nmaybe tens of supernovae"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934590,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would've blown all\nthis material outwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938100,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there are cosmic\nexplosions that are even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940620,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more deadly than normal\nsupernovae, gamma ray bursts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944640,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gamma ray bursts were discovered\nby the Vela satellites,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947670,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which were looking for\nSoviet nuclear tests"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950340,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but on the 2nd of July, 1967,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952860,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the satellites detected a\nlarge burst of gamma rays,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956400,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which were coming from space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959070,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two main sources\nof gamma ray bursts,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962070,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mergers of neutron stars\nand the core collapses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965340,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of gigantic stars called hypernovae."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968520,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hypernovae are caused by stars that are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970410,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least 30 solar masses\nand rapidly spinning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their collapse leads to an\nexplosion 10 times more powerful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978000,
    "dDurationMs": 4443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than a regular supernova, and\nit leaves behind a black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983490,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The gamma ray bursts caused\nby hypernovae channel most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987180,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their energy into beams"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988680,
    "dDurationMs": 2313,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are just a few degrees across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992040,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there was a gamma ray burst\nwithin 6,000 light years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995520,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would decrease the ozone level enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998280,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it could be catastrophic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000350,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To put this distance in\ncontext, a sphere with a radius"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003620,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 6,000 light years contains\nhundreds of millions of stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009380,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On October 9th, 2022,\nastronomers detected one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012620,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the most powerful gamma\nray bursts ever measured."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015620,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was powerful enough\nto measurably affect how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018020,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ionosphere bounces radio waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020810,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The effect on the ionosphere was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1022370,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around the same as a solar flare,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025280,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this gamma ray burst was located"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027530,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a galaxy 2.5 billion light years away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032300,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Astronomers speculate\nthat a gamma ray burst"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034610,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could have caused the Late\nOrdovician mass extinction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037490,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which wiped out 85% of marine\nspecies 440 million years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043160,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no direct evidence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045110,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but gamma ray bursts are common enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047810,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it is estimated that there has been"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a 50% chance that there was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an ozone-removing, extinction-causing GRB"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054320,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the vicinity of Earth in\nthe last 500 million years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058340,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if a supernova or\na gamma ray burst were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061160,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to go off near the earth now,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063170,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would be pretty catastrophic\nbut in an ironic twist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067370,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we kind of owe our\nexistence to these sorts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070880,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of explosions because\n4.6 billion years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074930,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was probably the shockwave\nfrom a nearby supernova"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078500,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which triggered the\ncollapse of a cloud of gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1082010,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and dust that gradually coalesced\nto form our solar system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086750,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the sun, the earth and all\nof us wouldn't be here today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091910,
    "dDurationMs": 3648,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without the explosions of nearby stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102710,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Figuring out how supernova\nexplode was incredibly difficult."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105980,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It took a combination of astrophysics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107810,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particle physics, computer\nscience and mathematics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110630,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you wanna develop\na better understanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112670,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our universe, then you should check out"
    } ]
